## honest boundary notes

- the composed run shells out to the same CLI paths (bash "$SELF" <mode>), so a section tally IS that solo mode tally by construction; the receipts also measure each solo mode separately for the reader to compare.
- an absent section is reported state=absent and never drifts by itself; the omission rule is the round-6 claim and its limit (a Chain-less record cannot compose CLEAN) is the named r7 candidate.
- a section that cannot be run inside verify-all (rc outside 0/1 or a summary the parser cannot read) is FINDING VERIFY_ALL_SECTION_UNAVAILABLE severity=crit and drifts the composition; not exercised by these fixtures.
- manifest lines append with >> (no rewrite path); a replayed line is information, not deduplicated — replay handling is not part of this round.
